{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsrc=open('explore_recvbal_test.go').read()\nclaim={\n \\\"id\\\":\\\"C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"concern\\\":\\\"consensus_safety\\\",\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"When recovery runs for instance (Replica, Instance) and a slow-quorum PrepareReply reports that instance COMMITTED with a command vector, the recovering replica must adopt that committed vector (Status COMMITTED carrying the committed commands) rather than continuing from its own record and restarting phase 1 with a different command.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Recovery decision for a single instance on the captured snapshot: N=3 with Thrifty and IsLeader false, the recovering replica holding only a default NONE record, one peer holding a COMMITTED record with a real command, and no third replica reply required.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"the recovering replica's own record carries no commands\\\",\\\"a slow quorum (its own entry plus one reply) is sufficient to resolve\\\",\\\"messages are delivered through the real wire format\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"producing the committed record through a real proposal, accept round and commit broadcast\\\",\\\"execution of the instance and client-visible replies\\\",\\\"configurations with N>3 or a live leader flag\\\"]},\n \\\"pending\\\":[]\n}\nb1={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB1-recovery-start\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"startRecoveryForInstance\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1127,\\\"end_line\\\":1169,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Recovery entry that seeds the leader bookkeeping from the local record, makes the new ballot and reports the record's vbal in its own PrepareReply.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The entry decides which vbal the recovering replica reports and therefore which remote replies the resolution may adopt.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nb2={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB2-prepare-resolution\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1204,\\\"end_line\\\":1314,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Resolution of PrepareReply values: highest-vbal selection, status-based sub-case choice and the restart of phase 1.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The loop applies element.VBallot >= lb.ballot and assigns lb.cmds/lb.status from the passing element, so a COMMITTED reply is only adopted when it passes that test; otherwise the resolution falls to the phase-1 restart.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nground={\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\"],\n \\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB1-recovery-start\\\",\\\"BB2-prepare-resolution\\\"],\n \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The obligation follows from the role of recovery in EPaxos: the value that could have been committed is the one with the highest vbal among a slow quorum, and a reply reporting COMMITTED is authoritative for the instance. The harness fixes the recovering replica's record as a default NONE record so the only value in the history is the peer's committed vector.\\\",\n \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"N=3, Thrifty, IsLeader false, one COMMITTED reply and one local default record; the recovery is entered directly through startRecoveryForInstance.\\\",\n \\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"whether a full legal history (proposal, accept round, commit broadcast, execution timeout) reaches the same state\\\",\\\"whether the launched configuration permits the recovering replica to be in that state at all\\\"],\n \\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}\nplan={\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: with the recovering replica holding only a default record for (1,0) and a peer reporting the instance COMMITTED at vbal 0, does the recovery adopt the committed vector or restart phase 1? Prefix: the peer's record is prepared as COMMITTED with a real PUT command; the recovering replica's record is a default NONE record; the peer's real PrepareReply is delivered through the real wire form. Controls: the same harness also prints the seed state (lb.ballot and the self VBallot) and which message the recoverer emits next, so an unreached prerequisite is visible rather than silent.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":claim[\\\"id\\\"],\n \\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB1-recovery-start\\\",\\\"BB2-prepare-resolution\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":src,\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test building two real Replica values and delivering Prepare/PrepareReply through their real Marshal/Unmarshal form.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"committed_reply\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"peer_committed_reply\\\",\n     \\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"COMMITTED\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"has_command\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":ground},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-recovery-resolution\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-recovery-adopts-committed\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"recovery_resolution\\\",\n   \\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB2-prepare-resolution\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB2-prepare-resolution\\\"],\n     \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The resolution event is the completed recovery decision for the instance: it records whether the committed vector was adopted, the resulting local status and which message the recoverer emitted.\\\",\n     \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Resolution reached with the prerequisite reply present for the same instance identity.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"committed_reply.instance\\\"}],\n   \\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"committed_reply\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-recovery-adopts-committed\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\n   \\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"recovery_resolution\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"adopted_committed\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"instance\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A completed recovery resolution in which a reply reported the instance COMMITTED must adopt that committed vector.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"The harness prepares the peer's COMMITTED record directly; a full history is not constructed.\\\",\\\"Only the resolution decision is observed, not the later accept round or execution.\\\"]\n}\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-recovery-adopts.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Formal check for the recovery-vbal Candidate: the exploration reproduced the mechanism in a clean copy, so this product fixes the requirement and the oracle. The obligation is that a slow-quorum reply reporting the instance COMMITTED must be adopted by the recovering replica; the harness reaches the resolution with a prepared COMMITTED peer record and a default local record and emits canonical events, and the monitor decides whether the resolution adopted it. The plan names the two bindings that carry the requirement (the recovery entry and the resolution loop) so the check can be reviewed against the encoded predicate rather than only against its output.\\\",\\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-recovery-adopts.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_recvbal_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"candidate\\\":{\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The obligation and bindings are supplied together with the check so the claim exists before the plan references it; the requirement is a recovery duty, not the earlier fast-path question.\\\",\\\"action\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\":{\\\"audit_spec_version\\\":4,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"ready_for_check\\\",\\\"preferred_check\\\":\\\"direct_test\\\",\n   \\\"question\\\":\\\"When recovery runs for instance (Replica, Instance) and a slow-quorum PrepareReply reports that instance COMMITTED with a command vector, does the recovering replica adopt that committed vector, or does it continue from its own record and restart phase 1 with a different command (NOOP when its record has no commands)?\\\",\n   \\\"importance\\\":\\\"If the committed vector is not adopted, the replicas that already committed and possibly executed the instance keep it while the recovering replica re-proposes another command, so the instance has two competing values: an installed commit that ignores later Commits versus a re-proposal that can be accepted by replicas that do not hold the commit. That is an agreement and state-convergence concern for a crash-recovered replica.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S6-conflicts-watermarks\\\"],\n   \\\"contexts\\\":[\\\"N=3 with Thrifty\\\",\\\"recovering replica holding a default NONE record\\\",\\\"peer holding COMMITTED with a command\\\",\\\"recovery entered directly through startRecoveryForInstance\\\"],\n   \\\"event_paths\\\":[\\\"startRecoveryForInstance seeds the local record and reports the new ballot as its own VBallot\\\",\\\"the peer's PrepareReply reports Status COMMITTED at an older vbal\\\",\\\"handlePrepareReply resolves and either adopts the committed vector or restarts phase 1\\\"],\n   \\\"activity_classes\\\":[\\\"A2\\\"],\\\"behavior_ids\\\":[\\\"B9-recovery-trigger\\\"],\\\"fact_ids\\\":[\\\"F6-ballot-priority\\\"],\n   \\\"supporting_behavior_ids\\\":{\\\"B11-prepare-resolution\\\":\\\"the highest-vbal selection and sub-case dispatch that decides adoption\\\",\\\"B6-commit-install\\\":\\\"shows what a committed replica reports\\\",\\\"B10-prepare-acceptor\\\":\\\"shows the Ballot/VBallot a remote replica reports after joining the new ballot\\\"},\n   \\\"obligation_relation_kind\\\":\\\"recovery\\\",\\\"priority\\\":3,\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"scoped to the source: the resolution rule compares element.VBallot against a running lb.ballot seeded from the record's old vbal while the self PrepareReply reports the new ballot, so the comparison order decides adoption (S14-recovery-start-prepare, S15-handlePrepareReply)\\\",\n     \\\"scoped to the launched configuration: makeBallot can also return a ballot below a remote vbal that was raised by an earlier recovery, which would change which replies pass the test (S5-broadcasters, S24-runReplica-epaxos)\\\"],\n   \\\"unknowns\\\":[\\\"whether a full legal history reaches the same state\\\",\\\"whether the recovering replica's accept phase can still complete when the committed replica refuses to store the new attributes (S11-handleAccept, S12-handleAcceptReply)\\\"],\n   \\\"trigger_rationale\\\":\\\"The exploration run in a clean copy showed the recovering replica reporting the new ballot as its own VBallot, skipping the peer's COMMITTED reply at vbal 0 and restarting phase 1 with NOOP; this check fixes that observation as a requirement with an explicit oracle.\\\"},\n  \\\"obligation\\\":claim,\\\"bindings\\\":[b1,b2]}}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-check.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written', len(plan['harness']['source']))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
